cant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, AKIKO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIRAO KAZUTAKA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MADONO MASAMI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MIE MASANORI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OJIMA NAOTO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO AKIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIRAO, KAZUTAKA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MADONO, MASAMI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIE, MASANORI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OJIMA, NAOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, AKIKO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A composition which is obtained by causing a specific compound to be present together with sucralose. The composition provides a sucralose in a stable form, more particularly, a sucralose which is still stable and thus is significantly suppressed with respect to the decrease in sweetness and discoloration (browning, blackening), even when it is subjected to a warming treatment under a condition wherein temperature is high and especially water content is low and/or pH is low. The stabilized sucralose-containing composition can be used as a sweetener by itself and as a compound with a food or a drug.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Composition obtenue au moyen de la mise en présence d'un composé spécifique avec du sucralose. Cette composition contient un sucralose sous une forme stable et plus particulièrement un sucralose qui est encore stable et par conséquent ladite composition ne subit sensiblement pas de réduction du goût sucré et ne subit pas de décoloration (brunissement, noircissement) même lorsqu'elle est soumise à un traitement de chauffage dans des conditions où la température est élevée et plus spécifiquement la teneur en eau est faible et/ou le pH est faible. La composition contenant du sucralose stabilisé peut être utilisée en tant qu'édulcorant en soi et en tant que composé lorsqu'elle est associée à un aliment ou un médicament.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>